.Dd $Mdocdate: September 22 2026 $
.Dt FUGUBENCH 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm fugubench
.Nd outfit a FuguBSD checkout for a coding agent
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm fugubench
.Op Fl h
.Op Fl C Ar dir
.Op Fl Fl verbose
.Ar verb
.Op Ar argument ...
.Nm fugubench
.Cm deps
.Op Fl Fl dry-run
.Op Fl Fl os Ar name
.Op Fl Fl arch Ar name
.Cm tool | runtime | test | develop
.Nm fugubench
.Cm deps Fl Fl update-sums
.Op Fl Fl force
.Op Fl Fl os Ar name
.Op Fl Fl arch Ar name
.Nm fugubench
.Cm doctor
.Op Fl Fl fix
.Nm fugubench
.Cm fetch Ar file url
.Nm fugubench
.Cm hook install
.Nm fugubench
.Cm hook SessionStart | SessionEnd
.Nm fugubench
.Cm hook WorktreeCreate | WorktreeRemove
.Nm fugubench
.Cm install
.Nm fugubench
.Cm shim
.Nm fugubench
.Cm traces
.Op Fl Fl root Ar dir
.Op Fl Fl name Ar name
.Nm fugubench
.Cm update
.Op Fl Fl version Ar tag
.Op Fl Fl allow-downgrade
.Nm fugubench
.Cm version
.Nm fugubench
.Cm wiki init
.Nm fugubench
.Cm wiki open Ar project session
.Nm fugubench
.Cm wiki note | admit Ar page file
.Nm fugubench
.Cm wiki close Ar session
.Nm fugubench
.Cm wiki status | candidates
.Nm fugubench
.Cm worktree create Ar name
.Nm fugubench
.Cm worktree remove
.Op Fl Fl force
.Ar name
.Nm fugubench
.Cm worktree list
.Nm fugubench
.Cm worktree clone Ar path ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
outfits a FuguBSD checkout for a coding agent.
It installs the dependencies that a repository names, and it makes and
removes the worktrees of a workspace.
It operates the learning library, answers the Claude Code hooks, and
measures the sessions.
One verb serves each concern.
.Pp
The program is one file.
It runs on core perl 5.34, and it loads no CPAN module.
One packed file carries the Fugu modules that it uses, so a host needs
no installed Fugu.
.Pp
A verb operates one checkout: the repository that holds the manifests,
the worktrees, or the library clone.
The program walks up from the start directory to the nearest directory
that holds
.Pa .toolingrc ,
and that directory is the checkout root.
The start is the
.Fl C
value, or the payload
.Ql cwd
of a hook, or the current directory.
A verb that needs a configuration key walks on to the nearest
.Pa .toolingrc
that holds the key.
The walk stops at the filesystem root.
A walk that reaches no
.Pa .toolingrc
names the start directory and gives a configuration error.
A worktree holds a
.Pa .toolingrc
of its own, so a worktree is a checkout of its own.
.Pp
Six verbs run no walk.
.Cm deps
reads
.Pa deps/<OS>.txt
relative to the start directory, because a guest runs it out of an
extracted tarball.
.Cm version , shim , install , update
and
.Cm fetch
read no checkout at all, so each one runs in a home with no
.Pa .toolingrc .
.Pp
Standard output carries the result of a verb only.
Every diagnostic, and every line of a child command, goes to standard
error.
A hook reads standard output, so a git message never reaches it.
.Pp
.Nm Fl Fl help
and
.Nm Ar verb Fl Fl help
print the usage to standard output and exit 0.
A usage error prints the usage to standard error and exits 2.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl C Ar dir
Read
.Ar dir
as the checkout root, in front of the walk above.
.It Fl h , Fl Fl help
Print the usage message and exit.
.It Fl Fl verbose
Trace each child command on standard error.
A verb can add its own progress lines to that stream.
.El
.Pp
The verbs are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm deps Oo Fl Fl dry-run Oc Ar environment
Install one dependency environment from
.Pa deps/<OS>.txt ,
where the file name holds the system name of
.Xr uname 1 .
The environments are
.Cm tool , runtime , test
and
.Cm develop .
A manifest line holds an environment, a type, and a name.
The types are
.Cm pkg , dist , cpan
and
.Cm bin ,
and the verb installs them in that order.
A
.Cm pkg
entry reaches the package manager of the platform, a
.Cm dist
and a
.Cm cpan
entry reach
.Xr cpanm 1 ,
and a
.Cm bin
entry lands in
.Pa ~/.local/bin
with mode 755.
Without a manifest for the system, the verb reports that fact and
exits 0.
.Pp
The verb holds each download to a digest.
.Pa deps/SHA256.txt
records a digest for each versioned download.
Without a recorded digest, the verb fetches the signed
.Pa SHA256
manifest beside the file, proves it under the keys of
.Pa deps/KEYS.txt ,
and holds the file to the digest of that manifest.
An entry with no recorded digest and no signature stops the install,
and a failed check stops the install at once.
The proof runs in process, so the host needs no
.Xr signify 1 .
.Pp
.Fl Fl dry-run
prints each command to standard output, and runs none of them.
.Fl Fl os
and
.Fl Fl arch
replace the two words of
.Xr uname 1 ,
which a manifest writes as
.Ql {os}
and
.Ql {arch} .
.It Cm deps Fl Fl update-sums Op Fl Fl force
Record the digest of each versioned download of the manifest in
.Pa deps/SHA256.txt .
The operator runs this command, and the install path never runs it.
The command skips a stable name, and a URL that a signed manifest sits
beside.
.Fl Fl force
rewrites a recorded digest, pins a stable name, and overrides the test
for a signed manifest.
A run that records nothing leaves the file as it was, and says so.
.It Cm doctor Op Fl Fl fix
Report the state of the checkout, as one
.Ql ok <check>: <detail>
or
.Ql problem <check>: <detail>
line for each check.
The checks are the version of the program, the presence of
.Xr git 1 ,
.Xr make 1
and a downloader on
.Ev PATH ,
the hook entries and the worktree base reference of
.Pa .claude/settings.json ,
and the state of the library clone.
The verb exits 1 when it wrote one problem line, so a make target can
gate on the report.
.Pp
.Fl Fl fix
skips the pending commit of a library clone that sits in a stopped
rebase, when that commit adds a session page with no observation.
It refuses every other stop.
.It Cm fetch Ar file url
Download one URL to one file, through the downloader of the program.
The file comes first, and the URL second.
A URL starts with a scheme, and a URL without one is a usage error.
.It Cm hook Ar event
Answer one Claude Code hook event.
The harness writes a JSON payload to standard input, and the verb
reads it.
The events are
.Cm SessionStart , SessionEnd , WorktreeCreate
and
.Cm WorktreeRemove ,
and another word is a usage error.
The checkout root comes from the payload
.Ql cwd .
The verb exits at once, with no change, when the payload holds an
.Ql agent_id
key, because a sub-agent sends that payload.
.Pp
.Cm SessionStart
runs
.Cm wiki init
and then
.Cm wiki open ,
and writes the page name to standard output as the only line.
.Cm SessionEnd
runs
.Cm wiki close .
A session event never stops a session: each failure warns and exits 0.
.Pp
.Cm WorktreeCreate
reads
.Ql cwd
and
.Ql name
from the payload, runs
.Cm worktree create ,
and writes the worktree path to standard output as the only line.
It fails when the worktree cannot be made, because the harness needs
the path.
.Cm WorktreeRemove
removes nothing.
It prints the path and the manual remove command to standard error,
and it exits 0.
.It Cm hook install
Write the four hook entries in
.Pa .claude/settings.json
of the checkout, and keep every other key of the file.
Each entry runs the shim of the checkout,
.Pa scripts/fugubench ,
and carries an explicit timeout.
The subcommand also sets
.Ql worktree.baseRef
to
.Ql head ,
because a worktree starts at the local HEAD.
A second run causes no change.
.It Cm install
Copy the running program to
.Pa ~/.local/bin/fugubench
with mode 755, atomically, and print the path.
The verb prints a hint when
.Ev PATH
lacks that directory.
.It Cm shim
Print the wrapper shim of a consumer to standard output.
The shim is POSIX shell, and a consumer keeps it at
.Pa scripts/fugubench .
It holds the download URL and the sha256 digest of the packed file of
the version that printed it, so the shim is the pin of the release.
The shim runs the cached file, or it downloads the packed file, holds
it to the digest, and caches it.
A checkout with no tag carries the version 0.0.0, and the verb refuses
such a version.
.It Cm traces Oo Fl Fl root Ar dir Oc Op Fl Fl name Ar name
Measure the Claude Code sessions of the checkout.
The verb prints one line for each session that holds a request, sorted
by start time, under a header.
The columns are
.Cm session , start , reqs , peak , out , panel , edits , sub-in ,
.Cm sub-out
and
.Cm rev-peak .
The verb reads the trace directory of the checkout, of each worktree
of it, and of each project clone in either.
.Fl Fl root
names a trace root in place of
.Pa ~/.claude/projects/ ,
and
.Fl Fl name
replaces the derived name.
.It Cm update Oo Fl Fl version Ar tag Oc Op Fl Fl allow-downgrade
Replace the running program with a verified release.
The verb fetches the
.Pa SHA256
manifest of the latest release, or of the named tag, and proves it
under the keys that the program embeds.
It then fetches the packed file, holds it to the manifest digest, and
replaces the running file atomically.
The result line is
.Ql fugubench <version> ,
and a failed update prints no line.
.Pp
The verb refuses a version below the running one, without
.Fl Fl allow-downgrade .
A replay of an earlier release is the attack that the refusal stops.
The verb also refuses to replace a file under the shim cache, and it
names the Tooling sync as the path to a new version there.
A key rotation can leave the program without the key of a later
release.
The verb then reports that no embedded key proves the signature, and
it names the install command.
.It Cm version
Print
.Ql fugubench <version>
and the Fugu version of the snapshot on one line.
A checkout with no tag gives the version 0.0.0.
.It Cm wiki init
Clone
.Ic wiki.origin
into the library directory when that directory is absent.
A second run causes no change.
A failed clone warns and exits 0, because a checkout without network
access is normal.
Each other subcommand reports an absent clone and exits 0, so the
library stops no session.
.It Cm wiki open Ar project session
Start the session page of
.Ar session ,
commit, and push.
The page name is
.Pa Session-<project>-<date>-<n>.md ,
and the verb writes it to standard output as the only line.
When a page holds the session identifier already, the verb prints that
page and changes nothing.
A push that meets a page of the same name at the origin makes the verb
rename its page to the next free index and retry.
.It Cm wiki note Ar page file
.It Cm wiki admit Ar page file
Append the text of
.Ar file
to
.Ar page
after one blank line, commit, and push.
The two subcommands differ in the commit subject only.
An empty file is an error.
A failed push warns and exits 0, and the commit waits for the next
push.
.It Cm wiki close Ar session
Append the
.Ql Closed:\&
line to the page of
.Ar session ,
commit, and push.
A second close changes nothing, and a session with no page is normal.
.It Cm wiki status
Report each open session with its page, its
.Ql Claim:\&
count, and its
.Ql Admitted:\&
count, and then the count of unpushed commits.
.It Cm wiki candidates
Report each undelivered candidate of the page
.Pa Rule-candidates.md ,
with its age in days and its date.
A candidate is a list item that starts with a date, and a
.Ql Delivered:\&
mark ends one.
The subcommand exits 0 when the clone or the page is absent, so a
checkout without a library passes its gate.
.It Cm worktree create Ar name
Make the worktree at
.Pa <root>/<worktree.base>/<name> ,
on a new branch
.Ar name
that starts at the local HEAD of the main checkout.
The verb then runs
.Ql make -C <worktree> bootstrap MAIN=<root>
when the worktree holds a makefile.
It writes the worktree path to standard output as the only line.
A second create of the same name runs the bootstrap again and exits 0.
A failed create leaves no worktree and no branch.
.It Cm worktree remove Oo Fl Fl force Oc Ar name
Remove the worktree of
.Ar name
and delete its branch.
Without
.Fl Fl force ,
the verb refuses a worktree that holds work at risk, and the message
names each cause.
The causes are an uncommitted change in the worktree or in a
repository inside it, and a commit that no remote holds.
The verb never deletes the branch
.Cm main ,
and never the branch of the main checkout.
Only an operator runs this subcommand, and no hook calls it.
.It Cm worktree list
Report each worktree with its name, its age in days, and its state.
The state is
.Cm clean ,
or each cause of
.Cm remove .
Without a worktree, the subcommand prints
.Ql no worktrees .
.It Cm worktree clone Ar path ...
Copy each gitignored
.Ar path
of the main checkout that
.Fl C
names into the current directory, with no network.
The subcommand makes a local clone of a git repository, clones each
child of a directory of repositories, and copies a plain file.
It copies each regular
.Pa .env
file of a cloned tree.
A destination that exists stays as it is, so a second run repairs a
partial bootstrap.
In the main checkout itself, the subcommand reports that fact and
changes nothing.
.El
.Sh CONFIGURATION
.Nm
reads its keys from
.Pa .toolingrc ,
the identity file of the synced FuguBSD tools.
A line holds a key, whitespace, and a value.
A
.Ql #
starts a comment.
The program ignores every other key of the file, because another tool
owns another prefix.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
wiki.origin   https://github.com/FuguBSD/Wiki.git
wiki.projects Projects
.Ed
.Pp
The keys are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width "wiki.projects" -offset indent
.It Ic wiki.dir
The library clone, under the home of
.Ic wiki.origin .
The default is
.Pa Wiki .
.It Ic wiki.origin
The URL of the library repository.
It has no default, and
.Cm wiki init
stops without it.
.It Ic wiki.project
The project name of a session at the root.
The default is the name of the root directory.
.It Ic wiki.projects
The directory whose children are project clones.
The default is
.Pa Projects .
.It Ic worktree.base
The directory of the worktrees, under the root.
The default is
.Pa .claude/worktrees .
.El
.Pp
The home of a key is the directory of the
.Pa .toolingrc
that holds it, and the root is the home of a default.
A
.Ic wiki.\&
value anchors at the home of
.Ic wiki.origin ,
and
.Ic worktree.base
anchors at the root.
A directory value is a relative path with no
.Ql ..
segment, and it names a directory below its anchor.
A URL value holds a scheme.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width "PERL_LOCAL_LIB_ROOT"
.It Ev FUGUBENCH
The program that the wrapper shim runs in place of the release.
A developer points it at
.Pa bin/fugubench
of a checkout.
A value that names no executable makes the shim report the value and
exit non-zero.
The shim tests for a set variable, so an empty value names no
executable either.
.It Ev FUGUBENCH_RELEASE_URL
The release address that replaces
.Lk https://github.com/FuguBSD/FuguBench
in each download of
.Cm update .
A test and a developer point the verb at another server with it.
.It Ev HOME
The home directory.
.Cm deps
stops with an error when a
.Cm bin
entry installs and the variable is unset.
.Cm update
refuses to run when the variable is unset or empty, because it cannot
find the shim cache then.
.It Ev PATH
The search path of each child command, and the list that
.Cm doctor
reads for
.Xr git 1 ,
.Xr make 1
and a downloader.
.It Ev PERL_LOCAL_LIB_ROOT
With a value,
.Cm deps
adds
.Fl Fl local-lib
with that value to each
.Xr cpanm 1
command.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "~/.cache/fugubench/<version>/" -compact
.It Pa .toolingrc
The configuration of the checkout.
.It Pa deps/<OS>.txt
The dependency manifest of one operating system.
.It Pa deps/SHA256.txt
The recorded digest of each versioned download.
.It Pa deps/KEYS.txt
The signify public keys of the organization.
.It Pa deps/KEYS.local.txt
The third-party keys of the consumer.
.It Pa scripts/fugubench
The wrapper shim of a consumer.
.It Pa .claude/settings.json
The settings file of Claude Code, which
.Cm hook install
writes.
.It Pa ~/.local/bin/fugubench
The program that
.Cm install
copies.
.It Pa ~/.cache/fugubench/<version>/
The shim cache of one release.
.It Pa ~/.claude/projects/
The default trace root of
.Cm traces .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm
exits with one of the following values:
.Pp
.Bl -tag -width Ds -offset indent -compact
.It 0
Success.
.It 1
A failure.
.Cm doctor
also gives this status for a report that names a problem.
.It 2
A usage error.
.It 3
A configuration error: no
.Pa .toolingrc
above the start directory, or a key that no file holds.
.El
.Pp
No verb defines another code.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Outfit a checkout, install the hooks, and read the report:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ fugubench deps tool
$ fugubench deps test
$ fugubench hook install
$ fugubench doctor
.Ed
.Pp
Make a worktree, list the worktrees, and remove it again:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ fugubench worktree create bugfix/parser
/home/dick/FuguBench/.claude/worktrees/bugfix/parser
$ fugubench worktree list
bugfix/parser                               2 d  clean
$ fugubench worktree remove bugfix/parser
.Ed
.Pp
Open a session page, add one observation, and close the session:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ page="$(fugubench wiki open FuguBench 4f21c0)"
$ fugubench wiki note "$page" observation.txt
$ fugubench wiki close 4f21c0
.Ed
.Pp
Run the checkout in place of the release that the shim pins:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ FUGUBENCH=$PWD/bin/fugubench scripts/fugubench version
fugubench 0.0.0 (Fugu 0.5.0)
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr cpanm 1 ,
.Xr curl 1 ,
.Xr ftp 1 ,
.Xr git 1 ,
.Xr make 1 ,
.Xr perl 1 ,
.Xr signify 1 ,
.Xr wget 1
.Pp
The module documentation is in the
.Pa .pod
sidecars beside
.Pa lib/App/FuguBench/ .
